      "question2": "What are the main differences between these two sports?",
      "question2_answer": "Football and high jump differ in team size, movement and scoring.\nFootballers work together for a full match and score by putting the ball into a goal.\nA high jumper performs alone and tries to clear a bar at a greater height.\nEven so, both sports require fitness, practice, confidence and the ability to perform well under pressure.",
      "question3": "Why are some sports more popular or important than others?",
      "question3_answer": "Some sports become more popular because they are easy to play, widely shown on television or connected to national success.\nFootball needs only a ball and an open space, so many children can start it.\nOther sports may require special equipment or facilities, which limits access.\nPopularity does not mean one sport has more value for every person."
